    "pressure.cpu_stall_distribution": {
      "title": "CPU Stall Distribution",
      "body": "What is this?\nA grouped article for CPU stall samples, useful when runnable work exists but execution is delayed.\n\nWhy it matters\nCPU stall distributions capture scheduler pressure and contention better than a single average.\n\nHow to read\n- count: sample count\n- max: worst stall\n- buckets: whether stalls are brief or sustained\n"
    },
    "pressure.io_full_avg10": {
      "title": "io_full_avg10",
      "body": "What is this?\nThe fraction of the last 10 seconds where all non-idle tasks were stalled on I/O.\n\nWhy it matters\nThis is a strong sign that storage is the bottleneck, not just a noisy background signal.\n\nHow to read\n- Any non-zero value is bad.\n- Sustained elevation means the host is effectively I/O bound.\n- Pair it with writeback and diskstats to separate device saturation from workload bursts.\n\nNext check\nLook at nr_writeback and diskstats.active_devices."
    },
    "pressure.io_full_avg300": {
      "title": "io_full_avg300",
      "body": "Auto-generated first-pass article for pressure.io_full_avg300.\\n\\nType\\n- Float\\n\\nHow to read\\n- Track trend in Diff/Graph before deciding.\\n- Cross-check with related source-level guide and pressure/capacity metrics.\\n\\nNext step\\n- Use this as first-pass context, then drill into neighboring fields in the same source."
    },
    "pressure.io_full_avg60": {
      "title": "io_full_avg60",
      "body": "Auto-generated first-pass article for pressure.io_full_avg60.\\n\\nType\\n- Float\\n\\nHow to read\\n- Track trend in Diff/Graph before deciding.\\n- Cross-check with related source-level guide and pressure/capacity metrics.\\n\\nNext step\\n- Use this as first-pass context, then drill into neighboring fields in the same source."
    },
    "pressure.io_full_total": {
      "title": "io_full_total",
      "body": "Auto-generated first-pass article for pressure.io_full_total.\\n\\nType\\n- Integer\\n\\nHow to read\\n- Track trend in Diff/Graph before deciding.\\n- Cross-check with related source-level guide and pressure/capacity metrics.\\n\\nNext step\\n- Use this as first-pass context, then drill into neighboring fields in the same source."
    },
    "pressure.io_some_avg10": {
      "title": "io_some_avg10",
      "body": "What is this?\nThe fraction of the last 10 seconds where at least one task was stalled waiting for I/O.\n\nWhy it matters\nThis is the cleanest signal that storage latency is affecting tasks.\n\nHow to read\n- Rising dirty pages plus this metric usually means writeback is behind.\n- If it stays above zero, tasks are waiting on storage.\n- Spikes can come from log bursts or backup windows.\n\nNext check\nCompare with diskstats.active_devices and cpu_iowait."
    },
    "pressure.io_some_avg300": {
      "title": "io_some_avg300",
      "body": "Auto-generated first-pass article for pressure.io_some_avg300.\\n\\nType\\n- Float\\n\\nHow to read\\n- Track trend in Diff/Graph before deciding.\\n- Cross-check with related source-level guide and pressure/capacity metrics.\\n\\nNext step\\n- Use this as first-pass context, then drill into neighboring fields in the same source."
    },
